 {"acceptance_criteria":"Tier-2 grading must produce a graded verdict on a consensus row instead of a cap abort. REPRODUCED 2026-11-16 twice on this repo: QA-CONSENSUS-33 (verdict run af4510fb: 'Cap exceeded: Iteration cap (120) reached (121.0 used) ... 0 of 1 criteria graded', 1,302,708 in / 4,787 out) and DF-CONSENSUS-65 (2,023,828 in over 223.6 iterations, 0 of 1 criteria graded). Tier 1 passes normally (secrets/lint/spec_parity/tests) and each row's work was independently verified green by the foreman, so the defect is the evaluator's scoping, not the code under test. VERIFY: (1) state the root cause with evidence from a run log (candidates: file_scope=full re-sends the repo tree per iteration, spec_parity/test stages re-read large trees, no stop condition after N ungraded iterations); (2) a consensus row is graded end to end and writes criteria[].result with graded == N; (3) the fix bounds context per iteration (file_scope=diff, one criterion per run, or a hard per-criterion token ceiling) rather than only raising caps \u2014 raising max_iterations 60->120 (7abd30df) and max_input_tokens to 2M did not help. FAILIF any future consensus tier-2 run ends with '0 of N criteria graded' plus a cap message. A capped run must not be reported as a substantive FAIL \u2014 it means ungraded.\nVerify: one tier-2 run on a consensus row prints a graded verdict whose graded count equals the row's criteria count and no 'Cap exceeded' line, and `grep -c 'Cap exceeded' <the run's own verdict file, verdict.json, under the .gitreins history tree>` prints 0 for the run under test (proven 2026-11-21: capped run af4510fb greps to 4, healthy 2026-11-20 runs grep to 0); expected outcome is a substantive verdict, never '0 of N criteria graded'.","attempts":0,"branch":null,"capability_tags":["harness","gitreins","evaluator"],"ci_result":"GREEN","commit_hash":"51f14cec2b633835d686464b814c1aa6159ca7f0","complexity":3,"created_at":"2026-11-16T15:53:26Z","depends_on":[],"detail":{"metadata":{